WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.278 --> 00:00:05.217
How to find a developer.

00:00:05.217 --> 00:00:08.486
I got a great question from one of my YouTube visitors (Love you, guys!),

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:13.600
... Robell, who wrote in to say: "Very inspirational video, I need some help. I've got an idea and I have done...

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.432
the research on it, but the problem I have is finding a developer who can execute my product."

00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:22.138
This is a great question and for anybody who is in technology: Hey, we need developers to...

00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:23.781
... make things happen.

00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:25.270
Your 3 options are:

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.374
Find a business partner who is a developer.

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:29.083
Hire a local developer.

00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:31.544
Or get somebody to outsource it to.

00:00:31.544 --> 00:00:35.396
Ok, I'm going to go through the pros and cons of each and you can decide what's best for you.

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:40.650
The cheapest way is to go and outsource it, right? You find somebody who is, you know, in a different...

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.113
... country, has lower cost of living, the prices are lower.

00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:49.275
This is great when you have project-based work, when you don't need to see them face to face,

00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:53.574
... where you can be really specific on what you need to have accomplished... and it's great!

00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:56.208
One of my favorite websites to use for it is oDesk.

00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:59.719
I've hired a lot of great people on oDesk for lots of different types of projects,

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:02.404
... including Christina who edits all these videos.

00:01:02.404 --> 00:01:03.407
Hey, Christina!

00:01:03.407 --> 00:01:05.625
So it could be a great tool for you.

00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:12.417
What I really think you need to decide is: are you going to be a technology company or not? Ok?

00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:16.667
If you're going to be a technology company, then you need somebody on your team.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.885
It's not just having somebody local, face to face that you can meet with,

00:01:19.885 --> 00:01:24.971
... but you need somebody who is investing their heart and soul into this business to make it better.

00:01:24.971 --> 00:01:29.483
A buddy of mine runs a web-based business, technology based company,

00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:34.298
... and he's had some growth and success, but he's always been limited because he doesn't have a

00:01:34.298 --> 00:01:37.052
... dedicated tech person on his team.

00:01:37.052 --> 00:01:39.842
He doesn't have a CTO, a Chief Technology Officer.

00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:46.776
You need somebody who is dedicated to your business. Not just pay the salary, but is living and breathing

00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:49.132
... your company, just like you are.

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:52.463
IF you're going to be a technology company. So that's a big decision for you.

00:01:52.463 --> 00:01:58.834
Are you just launching a product that you need some build on, maybe some support on, that you can outsource

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:01.396
... or have somebody local that you can meet with face to face on?

00:02:01.396 --> 00:02:07.657
Or do you need somebody who is committed to this because you are really building a business

00:02:07.657 --> 00:02:09.846
... around products and technology?

00:02:09.846 --> 00:02:11.912
That's a really important decision! Ok?

00:02:11.912 --> 00:02:15.093
If you're going to outsource, my recommendation is oDesk.com.

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:17.941
Go check it out, you can post a job, you can interview people.

00:02:17.941 --> 00:02:21.742
You know, you put the through-trial jobs and see which one you work best with.

00:02:21.742 --> 00:02:26.456
If you're going to do a local hire, you know, you could put in the job posting.

00:02:26.456 --> 00:02:29.929
You could meet people face to face. You could do group interviews.

00:02:29.929 --> 00:02:33.332
I like doing group interviews first and then go into individual interviews.

00:02:33.332 --> 00:02:35.196
And you can find the programmer you need.

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:39.554
If you're looking for a business partner, it becomes trickier, because you need somebody

00:02:39.554 --> 00:02:42.264
... who believes in the same thing that you do, right?

00:02:42.264 --> 00:02:45.749
You have somebody who has the same values, who wants to build the same thing as you do.

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:49.286
The best way to do it is: you have to get out there and start talking to people.

00:02:49.286 --> 00:02:52.718
You've got to talk to your current network, your friends, your family.

00:02:52.718 --> 00:02:56.907
People you know, let them know what you're looking for, to know the kind of projects you're working on.

00:02:56.907 --> 00:03:02.713
And also go out and start hanging out at events. Go to meet-ups, go to industry events.

00:03:02.713 --> 00:03:07.186
Places where programmers will likely be and start telling them about what you're doing.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.019
And find somebody you can click with, right?

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:15.682
A business partnership is like getting married, you know? You're spending probably more time with them

00:03:15.682 --> 00:03:17.904
... during the week than you are with the person you married.

00:03:17.904 --> 00:03:24.034
So, you know, you need to have somebody that you can really, really, really get along with.

00:03:24.034 --> 00:03:28.836
Who, you know, it's not only good in the good times, but good in the bad times as well.

00:03:28.836 --> 00:03:33.374
So, you don't want to just rush into it. Start working on something small, see if you work

00:03:33.374 --> 00:03:35.708
... together well and expand from there.

00:03:35.708 --> 00:03:39.526
But your real decision is: do you need to build the technology company?

00:03:39.526 --> 00:03:43.260
Do you want somebody who is really going to be part of your team and help you build this thing up?

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.114
Or can you just offshore this or delegate it out to somebody to help you build?

00:03:47.114 --> 00:03:50.085
You figure that out, you're closer to being on your path.

00:03:50.085 --> 00:03:52.458
And that's how you find the right developer.

00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:53.293
Believe!

00:03:53.293 --> 00:03:55.666
For those of you watching, you liked the video? Thumbs up below.

00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:58.989
Let me know what you think, ask me a question underneath, leave a comment below,

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:03.784
... I'll make a video response. And if you want to see more videos like this, subscribe to my channel

00:04:03.784 --> 00:04:06.953
... by clicking on my face. Thank you so much! I'll see you soon.

